TITLE: YGGDRASIL TRAINING TRACK T6 / APPLICATION A14 — Bounded Novel-Context Discovery and Developmental Memory Creation
DATE: 2026-09-21
STATUS: PREREGISTERED / NOVEL-CONTEXT CREATION GATE / NON-CANONICAL
TRACK: YGGDRASIL TRAINING T6 / APPLICATION-A
PARENT: A12 T5 Latent Context Inference
BRANCH: dg1a-ar

PURPOSE

A12 established that Yggdrasil can infer which of two stored developmental memories applies
from recent experience alone,
and can abstain when neither stored memory matches.

A14 asks the next question:

WHEN EXPERIENCE REPEATEDLY MATCHES NO STORED DEVELOPMENTAL MEMORY,
CAN THE ORGANISM JUSTIFY CREATING EXACTLY ONE NEW BOUNDED CONTEXT SLOT,
LEARN ITS DEVELOPMENTAL PRIOR,
AND LATER RECOGNIZE / REUSE THAT NEW MEMORY
WITHOUT DUPLICATE CONTEXT PROLIFERATION?

BOUNDARY

Synthetic software only.

No living tissue.
No wetware.
No production deployment.
No network exposure.
No CKB / KTRADE integration.
No financial task.
No canonical DG-1R-05 execution.
No STAB-18-R1 execution.

NON-CANONICAL.

T6 CLAIM

A14 permits exactly one additional developmental context beyond A11/A12:

A;
B;
C.

Hard slot capacity:

3.

It does NOT permit:

unbounded context creation;
constitutional self-modification;
task-program mutation;
governance mutation;
provenance mutation;
repair-authority mutation;
automatic slot eviction.

