ROLE-PRIOR CATALOG

Carry forward A10-A12 exactly.

124 valid integer priors.

POST-FREEZE NOVEL PRIOR C

No primary C prior may exist before A14 freeze.

Let F13 be the exact A14 harness freeze commit.

For scenario s:

derive:

SHA-256(
"YGG-A14-PRIOR-C|"
+ F13
+ "|"
+ decimal(s)
+ "|"
+ decimal(counter)
).

Map into the frozen 124-prior catalog.

Reject only if:

candidate == prior_A
OR
candidate == prior_B.

No distance shaping,
difficulty shaping,
or post-freeze replacement is allowed.

Thus:

C != A;
C != B.

KNOWN-CONTEXT PRECHECK

Before novel-context discovery,
each scenario executes one known-context phase.

Known context:

A or B

derived from:

SHA-256(
"YGG-A14-KNOWN-PRE|"
+ F13
+ "|"
+ decimal(s)
).

Use the frozen A12 two-probe selector.

Required:

known context recognized in exactly two probes;
no new context slot proposed;
slot count remains 2.

NOVELTY ENTRY

The novel C phase begins with the A12 selector.

The first two C observations form an exact symmetric pair around prior_C.

Required after two unique observations:

A12 known-memory selector = ABSTAIN.

No slot creation.

No fallback to nearest A/B.

UNRESOLVED DWELL

A13 requires at least:

8 unique unresolved C observations

before novelty can even be nominated.

The first 8 C observations are:

4 exact zero-mean pairs around prior_C.

Before observation 8:

novelty_candidate = FALSE;
slot count = 2.

At observation 8:

if the exact mean belongs to the frozen prior catalog
and matches neither A nor B:

novelty_candidate = TRUE.

This nomination does NOT create a slot.

FULL DEVELOPMENTAL TRAINING WINDOW

After novelty nomination,
continue collecting C observations until:

64 unique observations

exist.

Use the same corrected zero-mean pair generator as A10/A11.

Exact mean over 64 observations:

prior_C.

No C evaluation demand is visible during training.

DISTRIBUTED MEMORY

Carry forward A09 distributed cellular observation memory.

Every C developmental observation is one causal observation identity.

Physical replication provides durability only.

Duplicate copies do not increase observation count.

No hidden central restore.

NOVELTY OBSERVATION PROVENANCE

Every unique C observation requires two independent observation attestations.

Observation roots:

O0 = 1 << 52.
O1 = 1 << 53.
O2 = 1 << 54.
O3 = 1 << 55.

For each observation,
derive two distinct roots post-freeze.

Both roots attest the same observed demand vector.

Admission requires:

2 distinct roots;
same observation digest;
same demand vector.

Same-root fanout never satisfies the two-root requirement.

This is observation provenance,
not evaluator truth.

NOVEL-CONTEXT LEARNERS

Two independent developmental learner lineages remain:

DEV_LEARNER_A_ROOT = 1 << 50.
DEV_LEARNER_B_ROOT = 1 << 51.

Each independently reconstructs the 64 admitted C observations from distributed memory
in separately derived deterministic orders.

Each computes exact arithmetic mean.

Required candidate:

prior_C exactly.

Learners may not share intermediate state.

CONTEXT SLOT CREATION AUTHORIZATION

A new C slot may be created only if:

slot count == 2;
novelty dwell >= 8 unique unresolved observations;
64 qualified unique C observations exist;
Learner A candidate == Learner B candidate;
learner roots are independent;
candidate belongs to frozen 124-prior catalog;
candidate != prior_A;
candidate != prior_B;
existing organism governance passes;
existing registry qualification passes.

New slot record:

slot_id = C;
version = 1;
role_prior = learned prior_C;
parent_digest = "NEW_CONTEXT_GENESIS";
policy_digest;
commit_epoch.

After creation:

slot count = 3.

HARD CAPACITY

Maximum developmental context slots:

3.

When slot count == 3:

no fourth slot may be created.

A novel D candidate must:

ABSTAIN / CAPACITY_BLOCKED.

No automatic eviction.

No implicit overwrite.

DUPLICATE-CONTEXT COALESCENCE

If an unresolved observation window reconstructs a prior equal to any existing slot:

do NOT create a new slot.

Instead:

coalesce to the existing slot identity.

Slot count remains unchanged.

No duplicate policy authority is created.

C1 HELD-OUT EVALUATION

After authorized C creation:

run 32 held-out C service epochs.

Generate 16 exact zero-mean pairs around prior_C
using a post-freeze evaluation generator independent from training.

Replacement episodes:

service epoch 0;
service epoch 16.

Each replaces four clean cells.

Candidate uses learned C prior.

BASELINE UNKNOWN-FALLBACK uses:

(3,3,3,3).

ORACLE uses hidden prior_C.

KNOWN-CONTEXT INTERLUDE

After C1:

run one known A/B phase,
using the opposite known context from the precheck.

A12 two-probe inference must still recognize that stored context.

C slot remains unchanged.

This tests that adding C did not damage A/B selection.

C2 RETURN / RECOGNITION

Then C returns.

No C retraining is allowed.

Use only:

2 new C context probes.

A12-style selector now compares against three stored slots:

A;
B;
C.

Required:

C selected in exactly 2 probes.

Then run a NEW 32-epoch held-out C2 service sequence.

Replacement episodes:

0;
16.

This proves:

novel discovery once;
later recognition/reuse without relearning.

