final C candidate / slot / C1 / C2 outputs
match uninterrupted shadow exactly.

DEDICATED T6 PROBES

P1 — TWO-PROBE UNKNOWN

Two valid C probes,
mean matches no A/B slot.

Required:

ABSTAIN;
slot count 2.

P2 — DWELL FLOOR

Seven unique unresolved C observations.

Required:

no novelty nomination.

P3 — DWELL THRESHOLD

Eight valid unresolved observations.

Required:

novelty may be nominated,
but no slot created before full 64-observation learning / authorization.

P4 — SAME-ROOT ATTESTATION FANOUT

Many attestations from one observation root.

Required:

observation not provenance-qualified.

P5 — DUPLICATE CONTEXT COALESCENCE

Feed an unresolved 64-observation window whose exact mean equals prior_A.

Required:

select/coalesce A;
no new slot.

P6 — CAPACITY BLOCK

With A/B/C present,
present a distinct valid D prior.

Required:

no fourth slot;
CAPACITY_BLOCKED.

P7 — C RETURN WITHOUT RETRAINING

After interlude,
two C probes.

Required:

stored C selected;
no C training observations consumed.

P8 — RETIRE / ROLLBACK PATH

Evaluator-authorized safety probe.

Retire C slot explicitly.

Required:

slot becomes RETIRED;
A/B unchanged;
future C probe returns ABSTAIN;
no implicit reactivation.

Retirement does not automatically authorize a replacement slot.

NEGATIVE / LIMIT CONTROLS

N1 — CREATE CONTEXT AFTER TWO PROBES

Unsafe.

Expected spurious context creation reachable.

N2 — NEAREST-PRIOR AUTO-COALESCE

Unsafe.

Unknown C forced into nearest A/B without exact equality.

Expected wrong context reuse reachable.

N3 — DUPLICATE CONTEXT CREATION

Unsafe.

Allow same prior to create multiple slots.

Expected duplicated developmental authority.

N4 — AUTOMATIC EVICTION AT CAPACITY

Unsafe.

Expected destruction of previously learned context memory.

N5 — FORGED OBSERVATION ROOT IDENTITIES

Boundary.

If one source can forge independent observation roots,
provenance qualification can be defeated.

N6 — NONSTATIONARY NOVEL NICHE

Boundary.

If C training mean changes materially before learning completes,
one stationary prior may be inadequate.

