PLAIN-SPEAK PREREGISTERED QUESTION

A12 can say:

"I recognize A."

"I recognize B."

or:

"I do not know this environment."

A14 asks what happens after:

"I do not know."

It is not allowed to invent a new developmental memory immediately.

It must keep watching.

After enough unresolved experience,
it may nominate the environment as genuinely new.

Then it still has to learn the new developmental pattern,
have two independent learners agree,
and pass normal governance before a new context memory exists.

Only one extra slot is allowed.

If the new environment is actually just A again,
it must reuse A instead of creating a duplicate.

If all three slots are full,
it must stop rather than silently delete an old memory.

Finally,
after C has been learned once,
C disappears and later comes back.

Yggdrasil must recognize C from two observations
and reuse the stored developmental memory without retraining.

This tests the first bounded form of:

UNKNOWN
->
NOVELTY
->
LEARNING
->
AUTHORIZED MEMORY CREATION
->
LATER RECOGNITION AND REUSE.

